Package: assignmentB2SadilaJayasinghe
Title: Count Missing Values For All Columns By Group
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Sadila", "Jayasinghe", , "sjayasin@student.ubc.ca", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Given a data frame `data` and a column `group`, 
      `count_all_missing_by_group()` creates a new data frame with one row per level of `group`. 
      The first column of the output data frame contains the levels of `group`, 
      and the rest of the columns contain the number of missing values for all columns in `data` except `group`.
